  "phase3_gemini_self_healing": {
    "forensics": "The strategy is actually gross-profitable in Out-of-Sample testing (+\u20b923.39 Gross P&L), but statutory NSE transaction charges and brokerage (\u20b943.38) turned it net-negative (-\u20b919.99). Specifically, mid-morning entries (10:25\u201311:15 IST) in NTPC, INFY, and TATASTEEL suffered from 0.55%\u20130.65% noise whipsaws due to an overly permissive 1.8x volume filter, while late-afternoon entries (post-14:20 IST) in COALINDIA and ICICIBANK ran out of session time and suffered fee-drag losses upon EOD square-off.",
    "learning": "In low-capital NSE cash equity trading, sub-2.0x volume sweeps during the mid-morning liquidity lull and post-14:15 IST entries lack sufficient institutional momentum to overcome the ~0.15% round-trip statutory fee hurdle before either mean-reverting into tight 0.55% stops or hitting the 15:15 IST EOD square-off window.",
    "parameter_patch": {
      "min_target_pct": 1.45,
      "min_sweep_vol_multiplier": 2.2,
      "breakeven_trigger_r": 1.05,
      "min_sl_pct": 0.65
    },
    "plan_update_summary": "### Cycle #46 Post-Mortem & Parameter Mutation\nOut-of-sample forensics revealed that DeepSeek V4.1 Flash achieved positive gross expectancy (+\u20b923.39), with the entire net drawdown (-\u20b919.99) driven by \u20b943.38 in execution friction and mid-morning stop whipsaws. High-beta cyclicals (e.g., TATASTEEL) breached the 0.55% minimum stop floor within minutes of entry, while post-14:20 IST entries (COALINDIA, ICICIBANK) stagnated into EOD square-off, generating negative net returns despite flat-to-positive gross price action. To eliminate fee bleed and false breakouts, `min_sweep_vol_multiplier` is tightened from 1.8x to 2.20x to demand genuine institutional footprint, `min_sl_pct` is widened to 0.65% to absorb normal NSE 5-minute microstructure noise, `min_target_pct` is expanded to 1.45% to dilute fixed fee drag on winners, and `breakeven_trigger_r` is pulled in to 1.05R to defend open equity faster."
